      "body": "## Motivation\n\nWith pipeline parallelism on gfx950, `DeepseekV2Model.__init__` crashes on every stage that does not own the embedding:\n\n```\nAttributeError: 'PPMissingLayer' object has no attribute 'embedding_dim'\n```\n\nThe aiter gfx950 allocator sizing (`_use_aiter_gfx95 and config.n_routed_experts == 256 and ...`) reads `self.embed_tokens.embedding_dim` and `self.layers[i].mlp`, which are `PPMissingLayer` placeholders on stages that do not own them. Any 256-expert model of this family hits it, not only DeepSeek-V3: GLM-5.2 (`amd/GLM-5.2-MXFP4`, hidden size 6144) fails the same way as a `--tp-size 1 --pp-size 4` P/D prefill worker on MI355X with `lmsysorg/sglang-rocm:v0.5.22-rocm720-mi35x-20261018`, and only stage 0 comes up.\n\nThis is #21194 by @RolaoDenthu, approved by @ch-wan, rebased onto current main. Its first hunk no longer applies (the surrounding a2a sizing code changed) and its title fails the current title check; it has had no activity since March. The change is unchanged and credits the original author (`Co-authored-by`). Happy to close this in favor of #21194 if it gets updated.\n\n## Modifications\n\n`python/sglang/srt/models/deepseek_v2.py`: the four bare attribute reads in the gfx950 allocator block become `getattr` calls, as in #21194. On a stage without the embedding the 7168 check reads `None`, so the block is skipped there; the remaining reads only run when the condition holds.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNo numerical change: the edits only decide whether a stage that has no embedding enters this allocator block. For GLM-5.2 (hidden size 6144) the block is skipped on every stage either way. We have run GLM-5.2 PP4 prefill with an equivalent local fix (`config.hidden_size` in place of `embed_tokens.embedding_dim`) since Oct 21: GSM8K 0.9666 (strict) / 0.9674 (flexible) on 1P1D with real MTP acceptance, and 3,600-second AgentX runs on 1P1D, 1P + 4-GPU decode and 2P1D.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot affected.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit). (`ruff format` / `ruff check` 0.15.1 on the touched file)\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests). (model construction under PP on gfx950; covered by the run above, no CPU unit test)\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). (not needed)\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40810061554](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40810061554)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40810061795](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40810061795)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40810062070](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40810062070)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
